1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:03,760
(Amy:)Say, I heard an
interesting tidbit

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:05,110
(Amy:)about Howard and
Bernadette.

3
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:07,250
(Sheldon:)Really, Amy? Gossip?

4
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:08,980
(Sheldon:)I'm disappointed in you.

5
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:10,290
(Amy:)Now, now.

6
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:13,360
(Amy:)Evolutionary biologist Robin
Dunbar has identified gossip

7
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:15,760
(Amy:)as an aid to social
bonding in large groups.

8
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:19,430
(Sheldon:)Forgive my language,
but "poppycock."

9
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:20,460
(Amy:)What if he's right?

10
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:22,560
(Amy:)And by not
participating in gossip,

11
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:23,930
(Amy:)society breaks
down into

12
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:26,300
(Amy:)small feral bands of tattooed
motorcycle riders

13
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:28,650
(Amy:)fighting to the death over the
last few cans of tuna fish?

14
00:00:28,870 --> 00:00:30,070
(Sheldon:)Fine.

15
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:32,340
(Sheldon:)In the parlance
of the urban music scene,

16
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:34,980
"what's the 4-1-1"?

17
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:38,650
(Amy:)Bernadette is thinking about
breaking up with Howard.

18
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:41,480
(Sheldon:)I believe our nation's
tuna cans are safe.

19
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:44,720
(Sheldon:)Excuse me.
Dr. Greene, question?

20
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,590
(Greene:)Yes?

21
00:00:46,590 --> 00:00:47,970
(Sheldon:)You've dedicated
your life's work

22
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:49,990
(Sheldon:)to educating
the general populace

23
00:00:49,990 --> 00:00:52,530
(Sheldon:)about complex scientific ideas.

24
00:00:52,530 --> 00:00:53,800
(Greene:)Yes, in part.

25
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:55,330
(Sheldon:)Have you ever considered

26
00:00:55,330 --> 00:00:57,470
(Sheldon:)trying to do something useful?

27
00:00:59,570 --> 00:01:02,300
(Sheldon:)Perhaps, reading to the elderly?

28
00:01:02,310 --> 00:01:03,960
(Greene:)Excuse me?

29
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:07,540
Yeah, but not your books;
something they might enjoy.

30
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:11,280
(Sheldon:)I kid, of course. Big fan.

31
00:01:17,090 --> 00:01:20,720
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

